 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- Tool input is now automatically validated against its registered `inputSchema` before the tool's
+  executor is invoked. Validation failures are returned as a `ToolResponse` result describing
+  the missing or wrong-typed fields, which the chat orchestrator feeds back to the model for
+  recovery. Identifying values from rejected inputs are never echoed in results or logs.
+- Static tool definitions have their `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, throwing a
+  synchronous error naming the tool if the schema is invalid. Dynamic tool definitions have their
+  schemas compiled and cached by object reference on first use.
+
